fihrist:manuscript_11885 a mdhn:Manuscript ;
    rdfs:label "Add. 1569" ;
    dct:date "18th-19th cent." ;
    dct:description """This theological work, entitled ‘ Cyril ’ ቄርሎስ Qērellos ) in the Ethiopian
                            tradition, consists of a standard set of writings by Cyril of Alexandria and his
                            contemporary ecclesiastical counterparts including Theodotus of Ancyra , Severus of Synnada , Acacius of Melitene , Juvenal of Jerusalem , Rheginus of Constantina , Eusebius of Heraclea
                                Pontica , Firmus of
                                Caesarea , John of
                                Antioch , Epiphanius of
                                Salamis , Proclus of
                                    Cyzicus , Severian of Gabala , and Gregory of Neocaesarea . Translated from Greek
                            in the mid-first millennium, this work offers a unique witness to a
                            number of otherwise lost patristic works. Based upon a note on a front
                            flyleaves seeming to pertain to the convent of the Egyptian monk Serapion , it is most likely that this
                            particular manuscript came from Egypt ,
                            perhaps originally belonging to an Ethiopian monk resident at one of the
                            monasteries there.""" ;
    dct:identifier "manuscript_11885" ;
    dct:language "gez" ;
    dct:spatial "Egypt" ;
    dct:type "codex" ;
    mdhn:digitallyPublishedBy glam:publisher_Cambridge_University_Library ;
    mdhn:hasContribution contrib:manuscript_11885_person_102329138_aqt,
