    rdfs:label "Add. 1145" ;
    dct:date "undated. Probably 9th or 10th century AD /3rd or 4th century Hijri" ;
    dct:description "Fragment of an Abbasid Qur'ān probably written in the third or fourth century A.H. / ninth or tenth century C.E, containing the last three verses of Sura Luqmān (سورة لقمان), Sura al-Sajdah (سورة السجدة), Sura Al-Aʿzab (سورة الاعزب). The script seems to correspond to a mediocre version of the Abbasid Style B II as described by F. Deroche." ;
